WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back
to "Late Night."

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.268 line:92%
We're here with Don Johnson.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:05.472
Kenan Thompson is both
one of the warmest people

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
you could ever hope
to work with,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I also always found it
frustrating, as well.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.011 size:78% position:39% line:92%
The guy never misses.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every take,
he is just pitch perfect.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.682
And you watch, this year,
what he's doing at "SNL" -

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.549 line:92%
He's filming with you all week

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's coming back to "SNL"
without rehearsal,

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
nailing it there.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.822 size:75% position:38%
Are you as impressed
with Kenan as I am?

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Truly.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not
just actor goosh stuff.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is -- Doing a show
like this is not --

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.600 line:92%
[ Sighs ] Let's just face it

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not what you would
immediately expect

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.204 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Don Johnson to be doing.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.341 size:84% position:42%
And it was a little bit
of a risk, you know --

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
me coming in and taking on
this kind of a part and stuff.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, frankly,
Kenan is such a pro

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.217 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that he just --

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.254
He basically just catches me
and says, "Oh, no, you good.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:58.591
You know, props me back up
and says, "Keep it going."

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
I've actually developed

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
a kind of a thing here,
you know?

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.733 line:92%
And it's joyful, joyful, joyful,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:12.072
to come into work every da
and laugh -- and we laugh.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
And somehow,
I got Kenan's funny bone.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Chris Redd too,
for some odd reason.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:21.548
And maybe it's just becaus
I'm the crazy white guy.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-I don't know.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's nice to know
that it still has some currenc

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.787 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to be a crazy white guy.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:31.658
-Yeah, well, it's about the only
thing we really can own.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
So, let me ask you this,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:39.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you also had
incredible chemistry last year

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.667 line:92%
For my money, the best show.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.102 line:92%
I guess now it's two years ago

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.603 line:92%
Again, same thing as you.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.304 line:92%
Corona's mushed my brain.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:49.609
But you and Regina King were s
good together in "Watchmen."

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
That must have been
an incredible thing

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to be a part of.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.347 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It really was.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the funny thing
about "Watchmen"

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.418 line:92%
is that Damon Lindelof --

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:03.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
who took the original
source material of "Watchmen

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:08.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then made this
masterpiece, basically --

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:15.168 size:84% position:42%
He wrote me the most
gooshing, loving letter

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:15.802 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that you could ever get.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.770
And, of course, if you wan
an actor to do anything,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
you just send him a letter
that's like this --

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
telling him he's basically
the greatest thing

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.645 size:81% position:41%
since sliced bread --
and we'll do anything.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
And by the way,
I think I gave him

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.418 size:81% position:41%
one of his first jobs,
if not his first job.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.653 line:92%
He was on my writing staff

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:37.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he asked me if I'd com
and do him a favor.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I said, "Yeah!"

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.526 line:92%
You know, "Let me read it.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I read it,
and he wouldn't tell me

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.729 size:84% position:42% line:92%
anything more about it.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had no idea
I was a white supremacist.

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:47.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I had no idea

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.469 size:84% position:42%
that my grandfather was
a white supremacist.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a surprise
to all of us.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.008 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, anyway, yeah.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went down there,
and kind of simultaneously

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was shooting "Knives Out
with Daniel Craig

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:05.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that whole great cast
up there in Boston.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was back and forth
between Boston and Atlanta

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:11.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a very
fertile time, Seth.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] That's nice.
It's nice that you had
your fertile time

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
right before all of us
had to stop doing anything

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
It's good timing.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:22.268 line:92%
You talk about how sometimes

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:25.805 size:81% position:41%
a little sweet-talking
is helpful for actors.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:28.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were so great
in "Django Unchained" --

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.576 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Quentin Tarantino movie.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I heard tell
that he might have been

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of a bigger fan
of your work

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:37.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
and more knowledgeable of it
than even you were.

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, well,
he's more knowledgeable

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
of everyone's work.
-Right.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:46.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because Quentin is
a walking film historian.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.229 line:92%
And before I got the part,

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were at one of these joints
in L.A. somewhere

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
for an after party
of some sort.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he walked up to me
and he said,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:57.337 line:92%
"Do you know what, I just --

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what
I just loved you in?

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:02.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
I-I-I just loved you
in this movie that you did."

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"You know, that's great,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.178 line:92%
but I didn't do that movie."

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says, "Oh, yes,
you did that movie."

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I said, "No, no.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.717 line:92%
I've never heard of the movie.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.185 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I don't know the movie."

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
But anyway, he said,
"Oh, no."

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:16.556
And he started to tell me
the story of the movie

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
and name the people
that were in the movie

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:21.027 line:92%
and the DP and the director.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went...
[ Thumps hand ]

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, yeah!
I was in that movie."

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:28.468 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:30.303 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's fantastic!

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It was absurd.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.306 line:92%
I mean, I forgot, you know

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:36.209
-Yeah, well, that just speak
to the breadth of your career.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:39.512
You've got a couple in there
that you didn't even remember.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:42.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] There's a few
of them I haven't even seen.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your daughter Dakota is
obviously an accomplished acto

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
in her own right...
[ Stammers ]

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:47.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Who is that?

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Dakota.
We'll send you clips.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:50.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes!
-She's been on this show.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, the movie star Dakota
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:58.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
And let me just say, such
a fantastic talk show guest.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.100 line:92%
We always love having her here

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is just unique
and wonderful.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I wonder,
does she come to you

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
at this point in her caree
and ask for advice?

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or that is something
that happened decades ago?

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:11.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That bus left.
-Yeah.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That bus left.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
She doesn't need any
advice from me.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, she --

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the funny thing
about her is,

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:23.222
we have a rule in the family
that if you stay in school

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.090 line:92%
you get to stay on the payroll

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, if you go to college,
you get to stay on the payroll

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:30.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
And towards the end
of high school,

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:33.399
I went to her and I said,
"Um, so, do you want to go

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
visit some colleges
or something like that?"

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she went, "Oh, no,
I'm not going to college."

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I went, "Okay.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.709 line:92%
Well, you know what that means

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.611 size:84% position:42%
I mean, you won't be
on the payroll anymore,

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.014 line:92%
and how are you gonna manage?"

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she says,
"Don't you worry about it.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.254 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-And I said, "Eh, okay.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.689 line:92%
Well, what do you got in mind?

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said, "Just --"
[ Stammers, scoffs ]

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:02.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
Three weeks later,
she had nailed down that par

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
in David Fincher's
"The Social Network,"

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the rest is,
shall we say, cinema history

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:11.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, no, she doesn't really
call me for advice.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:17.143 line:92%
She calls me to say that,

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.178 line:92%
"Uh, gosh, I would see you

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:20.313 line:92%
but I've got three picture

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I'm shooting
at the same time."

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:24.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think
we all hope one day

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:28.755
our kids are successful enough
to not have time to call us.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.990 line:92%
-But she's gainfully employed,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.292 line:92%
and Seth, that's a great day

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:34.527 line:92%
-That's all you can ask for.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
I look forward
to that day myself.

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.965
Hey, Don, this has been an
absolute delight talking to you.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:41.667
It's equally delightful seeing
you and Kenan do your thing.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for making time
for us today.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, man.
It was a joy for me to be here

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you so much.

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:48.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Kenan" airs Tuesday nights
here on NBC.

